            <title>[ZEPPELIN-1727] Shift + enter runs two paras simultaeously in a particular case</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1727</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;scenario:&lt;br/&gt;
1. click &lt;b&gt;insert new&lt;/b&gt; in p1(say code in p1 is %sh date -u )&lt;br/&gt;
2. New para p2 is created and cursor is on the p2 editor.&lt;br/&gt;
3. Type code say %sh date -u and press shift + enter.(without clicking on  p2&apos;s editor)&lt;br/&gt;
The output of p1 and p2 will be same, p2 run triggered p1&apos;s run as well.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
